{
  "question_id": "q_076_prime_warehouse_storage",
  "slug": "prime-warehouse-storage",
  "title": "Maximize Prime Item Inventory",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "company": "Amazon",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "*Effective April 3rd 2024, we have updated the problem statement to provide additional clarity.*\n\nAmazon wants to maximize the storage capacity of its 500,000 square-foot warehouse by prioritizing a specific batch of prime items. The specific prime product batch detailed in the inventory table must be maintained.\n\nSo, if the prime product batch specified in the item_category column included 1 laptop and 1 side table, that would be the base batch. We could not add another laptop without also adding a side table; they come all together as a batch set.\n\nAfter prioritizing the maximum number of prime batches, any remaining square footage will be utilized to stock non-prime batches, which also come in batch sets and cannot be separated into individual items.\n\nWrite a query to find the maximum number of prime and non-prime batches that can be stored in the 500,000 square feet warehouse based on the following criteria:\n\nOutput the item_type with prime_eligible first followed by not_prime, along with the maximum number of batches that can be stocked.\n\nAssumptions:",
  "notes": [
    "Prioritize stocking prime batches",
    "After accommodating prime items, allocate any remaining space to non-prime batches",
    "Again, products must be stocked in batches, so we want to find the largest available quantity of prime batches, and then the largest available quantity of non-prime batches",
    "Non-prime items must always be available in stock to meet customer demand, so the non-prime item count should never be zero.",
    "Item count should be whole numbers (integers).",
    "The dataset you are querying against may have different input & output - this is just an example!"
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "inventory",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "item_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "item_type",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "item_category",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "square_footage",
          "data_type": "DECIMAL(10,2)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "inventory": [
      {
        "item_id": "1374",
        "item_type": "prime_eligible",
        "item_category": "mini refrigerator",
        "square_footage": "68.00"
      },
      {
        "item_id": "4245",
        "item_type": "not_prime",
        "item_category": "standing lamp",
        "square_footage": "26.40"
      },
      {
        "item_id": "2452",
        "item_type": "prime_eligible",
        "item_category": "television",
        "square_footage": "85.00"
      },
      {
        "item_id": "3255",
        "item_type": "not_prime",
        "item_category": "side table",
        "square_footage": "22.60"
      },
      {
        "item_id": "1672",
        "item_type": "prime_eligible",
        "item_category": "laptop",
        "square_footage": "8.50"
      }
    ]
  },
  "sample_output": [
    {
      "item_type": "prime_eligible",
      "item_count": "9285"
    },
    {
      "item_type": "not_prime",
      "item_count": "6"
    }
  ],
  "reference_sql": "WITH summary AS (\n  SELECT \n    item_type,\n    SUM(square_footage) AS total_sqft,\n    COUNT(item_id) AS item_count\n  FROM inventory\n  GROUP BY item_type\n),\nprime_calc AS (\n  SELECT \n    'prime_eligible' AS item_type,\n    FLOOR(500000 / total_sqft) * item_count AS total_items,\n    FLOOR(500000 / total_sqft) * total_sqft AS total_sqft_used\n  FROM summary\n  WHERE item_type = 'prime_eligible'\n),\nnot_prime_calc AS (\n  SELECT \n    'not_prime' AS item_type,\n    FLOOR((500000 - p.total_sqft_used) / s.total_sqft) * s.item_count AS total_items\n  FROM summary s\n  CROSS JOIN prime_calc p\n  WHERE s.item_type = 'not_prime'\n)\nSELECT item_type, total_items FROM prime_calc\nUNION ALL\nSELECT item_type, total_items FROM not_prime_calc;",
